GATE="secrets"
EXPECT_EXIT="1"
EXPECT_RULE="aws-access-token"
DESCRIPTION="Also asserts a denominator. EXPECT_SCANNED_MIN existed with no fault using it, so direction 2 asserted nothing about scope at all -- the mechanism added to catch a gate examining less than it claims was itself unexercised. A committed cloud credential must be caught. Expected rule is aws-access-token, with a FIXED identifier. The earlier expectation of generic-api-key, and the claim that gitleaks 8.30.1 fires no AWS-specific rule on a bare AKIA identifier, were both wrong: the rule exists and fires, but its entropy test means a randomly generated identifier triggers it only sometimes. Measured over ten random ids: aws-access-token twice, generic-api-key seven times, nothing once. So this fault was nondeterministic, and a fresh clone reported 26 proven 1 mismatched where the working tree reported 27 and 0. The exit code was right and the reason varied, which is the entire argument for asserting the rule and not only the exit code -- and for the fixture not being a dice roll."
EXPECT_SCANNED_MIN="2"
